                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            whenever the exponential exists. See
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Es"} Escardó, sections 8.1 and 10.2
            %a{:href => "#ELS"} ELS
            where it is shown that the natural topology on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X, Y)
            coincides with the topology of continuous convergence (which is the context for the theorem above).
          %p (Some applications of Arzela-Ascoli should also be given.)
          %h3#representability Representability
          %p It happens that the property of a family of functions being (uniformly) equicontinuous is equivalent to them defining a single function which is (uniformly) continuous.
          %p
            Recall that for a family of functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i : A \to B
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f : A \to B^I
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f(a)(i) = f_i(a)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
            are all (uniformly) continuous iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f
            is (uniformly) continuous when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^I
            is given the product uniformity.
          %p
            However, we can give
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^I
            another uniformity more analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/box+topology"} box topology
            of topological spaces. Specifically, the box power
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mo □
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^{\square I}
            is the uniform space with point set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \subseteq B^I \times B^I
            is an entourage iff there is some entourage
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi E
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \sim_E g
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^I
            and all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi G
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(i) \sim_G g(i)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mo □
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^{\square I}
            are generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^I
            for entourages
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            With this definition, we can see that the family of functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i : A \to B
            is (uniformly) equicontinuous iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mo □
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f : A \to B^{\square I}
            is (uniformly) continuous.
          %p
            This also gives a convenient way to show that an equicontinuous net of continuous functions which converge pointwise converges to a continuous function: a net of equicontinuous functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_d : A \to B
            gives a continuous function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mo □
                        %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B^{\square D}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_d
            converge pointwise, they converge to a continuous function.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              be a separated uniform space and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              a directed set, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi conv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} conv(D,B)
              be the subspace of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mo □
                        %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^{\square D}
              which contains the convergent nets. Then the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                    %mo :
                    %mi conv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim : conv(D,B) \to B
              which takes a net to the point it converges to is continuous.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi conv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} conv(D,B)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim M \in U \subset B
              be open. Then there is an entourage
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi lim
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E \circ E)[lim M] \subset U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi i
                    %mo .
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi E
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi conv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^D[M] := \{N \mid \forall i. M(i) \sim_E N(i) \} \subset conv(D,B)
              is a neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in E^D[M]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi lim
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim N \in \widebar{E[lim M]}
              (as all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(i)
              are in this closed set), so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi lim
                      %mi N
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi \
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim N \in \widebar{E[x]} \subseteq \(E \circ E)[x] \subseteq U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim
              is continuous at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
